From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:39:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: panel: samsung,sofef01-m: Allow
 vci-supply on ams605dk01
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Xperia 10 VI powers its ams605dk01 panel's DisplayIC from a 3.0V
supply, as the Xperia 5 does its amb609tc01: the phone's own device tree
lists vci next to vddio among the panel's supplies, fed by PM6150L's
LDO4. Allow describing it for that panel.

It stays optional there, as nothing is known about the Xperia 10 V's
board, which carries the same panel.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 .../bindings/display/panel/samsung,sofef01-m.yaml      | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/samsung,sofef01-m.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/samsung,sofef01-m.yaml
index bccc667aa..d990ee160 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/samsung,sofef01-m.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/samsung,sofef01-m.yaml
@@ -62,7 +62,15 @@ allOf:
     then:
       required:
         - vci-supply
-    else:
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            enum:
+              - samsung,sofef01-m-ams597ut01
+              - samsung,sofef01-m-ams597ut04
+              - samsung,sofef01-m-ams597ut05
+    then:
       properties:
         vci-supply: false
 
